Subject: Figures longer than a page (Latex)

I have a figure longer than one page that I have split myself so that it =
can
fit into 2 pages. However, Latex does not put the figures in adjacent =
pages.
Instead it treats them as 2 separate figures and puts them in different
(non-adjacent) pages. Is there a way of forcing Latex/Tex to force these =
the
2 (sub)figures to appear consecutively. Alternately, is there a way to =
handle
figures (floats in general) that extend beyond one page. Any help or =
pointers
will be greatly appreciated.

Rajeev
(rajeev@acura.ece.cmu.edu)
